::Q1::What is the role of a source system in a data warehouse architecture?
{ 
~It is the final reporting dashboard shown to users
~It is the schema used only for dimension tables
~It is the storage engine that always performs every transformation
=It is a system from which data is collected for analytical use
}

::Q2::What is the purpose of an ingestion or staging layer? 
{
~To provide end-user authentication only
~To replace all analytical queries with manual reports
=To receive and prepare incoming data before it is processed into the warehouse
~To permanently delete source records after extraction
}

::Q3::What does a semantic or reporting layer generally provide? 
{
~Raw network packets for application debugging
~A replacement for data ingestion
=Business-friendly access to analytical data for reports and analysis
~Physical hardware for source databases
}

::Q4::Why might a staging area retain data temporarily?
{ 
~It permanently replaces the warehouse
~It prevents any data validation from occurring
=It provides a controlled place to receive and prepare data before loading or transforming it
~It is intended to be the final user-facing report
}

::Q5::Which architectural goal helps protect operational systems from heavy analytical workloads? 
{
~Preventing analytical queries from using stored data
~Deleting historical data after each report
=Separating analytical processing from systems that handle day-to-day transactions
~Running every analytical query directly against every transaction record
}